          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Score as few points as possible. The round ends when a player hits 13 or 21 penalty points.',
          gameplay: "1. **Forced Capture**: If you hold a card that CAN capture a card or sum from the table, you MUST capture it. You cannot choose to discard if a capture is possible.\n2. **Building**: You can 'build' onto table cards to avoid a current capture, but you must be able to capture the build yourself on a future turn.\n3. **Table Clearing (Tabbe)**: Clearing the table is worth -1 point (a good thing in misere).",
          keyRules: [
            'Forced capture rule: must capture if possible',
            '10 of Diamonds (Storan) = 2 penalty points',
            '2 of Spades (Lillan) = 1 penalty point',
            'Each Ace = 1 penalty point',
            'Most Cards = 1 penalty point',
            'Most Spades = 1 penalty point',
            'Tabbe (clearing table) = -1 point',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Prioritize dumping your middle-rank cards (7, 8, 9) early. These cards are the most likely to be forced into capturing sum combinations on the table.',
          intermediate: "The 'High Card Shield': Keep your face cards (J, Q, K) for as long as possible. Since they only capture other face cards by rank match, they are the 'safest' way to discard to the table without being forced to take a pile.",
          advanced: "Tactical Building: If there is a 5 on the table and you have a 5 (forced capture!), play a 3 on the 5 to 'Build 8'. This delays the capture. Hopefully, someone else will be forced to take the 8 before you have to.",
          tips: [
            "The 'Tabbe' (Table Clearing) is your best friend. Even if you take a few cards, a Tabbe removes 1 penalty point from your total.",
            "Watch the Spades. Since capturing the 'Most Spades' is a penalty, try to feed your Spades to your opponents by building sums they likely have.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
